{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "System 360 and OS360", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about IBM System 360.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify information about the history of software and its characteristics in simple spoken and written situations. Give information about software history, characteristics and methodologies.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Design a timeline since 1950.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Put the mainframe computers in the years they were launched. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Show the timeline to your partners. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I identify when the principal mainframe computers appeared. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I design a timeline. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I carry out a brief presentation about my timeline. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Tense of Verb Be in Negative Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>The verb <strong>to be</strong> is normally used to indicate the role or state of a person, to talk about characteristics when it goes with an adjective and to indicate location. This verb has the same uses in its <strong>past form</strong>.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>Unlike other verbs in the<strong> past form</strong>, to make the negative form with <strong>to be </strong>you only have to add the word not after it<strong>, </strong>as it works both as a verb and an auxiliary:</p> <p><i>That <strong>was not/wasn&rsquo;t</strong> the fastest computer back in those days.</i></p> <p>Notice how the <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">contraction</span> is made, all you need to do is to put the two words together (<strong>was + not</strong>) and replace the letter &ldquo;O&rdquo; in not by an apostrophe.</p> <p>Take a look at the following chart to see the <strong>negative past form</strong> of the verb <strong>to be</strong> with all the subjects:</p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Although these two early programming languages improved programming functions, there was not an actual operating system as we know it today. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, these computers were not error-free and problems were not so easy to solve, the peripherals performed poorly, their processor was slow and their communication capabilities were virtually nonexistent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, the concept of the operating system wasn't very well known, until the influential development of IBM's S/360. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center><b>VERB TO BE \u2013 PAST NEGATIVE FORM\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>SUBJECT\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>VERB TO BE\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>EXAMPLE\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>You, We, They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>were <b>not</b> (were<b>n't</b>)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>They <b>weren't</b> the best computers.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>I, He, She, It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<center>was <b>not</b> (was<b>n't</b>)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>I <b>wasn't</b> present when talked about that.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expression Abstraction in FORTRAN", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p><strong>FORTRAN</strong> (word derived from Formula Translation) is an all-purpose, imperative programming language which is used especially in numeric computation and scientific computing and has had a very big influence on computing and programming from the very beginning.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During the initial days of computing, programming was a very slow and discouraging activity that required every single step to be coded as a separate machine instruction. By 1953, seeing this situation, John W. Backus started the development of the <strong>Fortran</strong> programming language (the name being a contraction of FORmula TRANslation).</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">His team&rsquo;s objective was to create a compiler capable of producing efficient object code similar hand-written assembly code and <strong>Fortran</strong> was exactly what they were looking for. Programmers did not have to write hard-to-understand hieroglyphics when, for example, creating an instruction to divide two variables A and B and saving the result in C, they could now be written in a more natural and easy-to-understand statement like:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">C = A/B</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is what we know as <strong>expression abstraction</strong>, because mathematical expressions could be written very similarly to the way they appear in a textbook. The secret for <strong>Fortran&rsquo;s</strong> initial quick spread was that scientists were able to write programs to solve problems themselves, in a simple way and with limited access to professional programming knowledge. Another key aspect for its success was that a program written in <strong>Fortran</strong> could be moved to any computer with a <strong>Fortran</strong> compiler. &nbsp;</p>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mainframe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a very big computer, regularly the center of a system serving many users", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The IBM System/360 and OS/360 mainframe architecture mark the beginning of the modern computer industry. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "launch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to release, publish, or send forth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On April 1964, IBM launched the System/360, this model and the next versions of it, were the first successful family of computers ever.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "release", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to issue, publish, launch, broadcast or exhibit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: FORTRAN (\u201cFORmula TRANslator\u201d), the world's first actual computer language was released in 1954 and, thanks to John Backus's vision, its IBM developer, it allowed people to program computers with simple instructions similar to the English language and with mathematical formulas.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "distinct", "type": "name"}, {"content": "different from others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The IBM System/360 mainframe architecture is a set of distinct terms and rules that are instructions to build products.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "remain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to continue to be the same", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Each generation of mainframe computers includes improvements in architecture to remain stable, secure, and compatible with as many computing platforms as possible. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le02ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can understand written information about a successful family of computers. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can use vocabulary related to mainframe architecture. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write a simple text about the importance of mainframe architecture.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What were the most common characteristics of the first real computers?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " When did the mouse and the graphic features in a computer first appear?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left